# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads as the build context.
#
# THIS FILE MUST EXIST. Without it gcloud generates a default that pulls in
# `.gitignore`, and `.gitignore` excludes `/data/` — the 648 MB of caches, none
# of which is tracked in git. The upload would carry no `data/` at all and the
# build would fail at `COPY data/ ./data/` with "not found". The cache is
# deliberately untracked and deliberately deployed, and this file is the only
# place those two facts are reconciled.

.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/
.env

# The two files that make data/ 11 GB instead of 648 MB. Same reasoning as
# .dockerignore, applied one layer earlier: excluded here they are never
# uploaded, so the build context stays small as well as the image.
data/singlecell/*.h5ad
data/singlecell/*.h5ad.gz

# Outputs and local tooling. None of it runs in the container.
reports/
specs/
run_all.py
make_artifact.py
verify_*.py
bootstrap.py
deploy.ps1
deploy.sh
DEPLOY.md
*.tar.gz
*.tar.gz.sha256
